{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/persistence\/segmentstore"]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"roleHeading":"Structure","role":"symbol","title":"SegmentStore","symbolKind":"struct","externalID":"s:11Persistence12SegmentStoreV","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SegmentStore"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SegmentStore","kind":"identifier"}],"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Traffluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Persistence\/SegmentStore.swift#L47","fileName":"SegmentStore.swift"},"modules":[{"name":"Persistence"}]},"relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/RecordStore","doc:\/\/Persistence\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/Persistence\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"kind":"relationships","type":"conformsTo"}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/init(events:directory:byteBound:segmentByteCount:)"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Initializers"},{"title":"Instance Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/byteCount","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/directory","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/dropReports","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/pendingRecordCount"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Properties"},{"title":"Instance Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/append(_:)","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/synchronize()","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/takeRecoveredRecords()"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Methods"},{"title":"Type Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/defaultByteBound","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/defaultDirectory"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Type-Properties"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SegmentStore","kind":"identifier"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"overview"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let store = try SegmentStore(events: [SignedUp.self, CheckedOut.self])","let tracker = Tracker(store: store)","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: vendor)"]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Write-through."}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" A tracker’s worker writes each record as it reaches it, before publishing","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it, with one ","type":"text"},{"code":"write()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", off the tracking caller’s thread, so the record survives the app","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"crashing or being killed from then on. The store makes the log durable against","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"power loss too (","type":"text"},{"code":"fsync","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") once per batch, before the batch is delivered, and whenever","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/synchronize()","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" is called: call it, after the tracker’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"flush()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", as the app moves to the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"background or terminates.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"A record whose write fails (the disk is full, say) is kept in memory only, and reported as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/writeFailed(recordCount:timestamps:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"What is kept."}]},{"type":"text","text":" Only events of the types in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"events"},{"type":"text","text":", which conform to "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/BinaryCodable"},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Events of any other type are kept in memory only: they are delivered in this run like any"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"other, are never written, and produce no drop report, but are lost if the app ends first."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"A record’s context is not kept: a recovered record is in the top-level "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ServiceContext"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"as its span ended with the earlier run."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Deleting."}]},{"text":" A segment is deleted as a whole once every record in it is delivered, so a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"log whose records are all delivered holds no files. There is no compaction: a segment kept","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"for one undelivered record keeps its delivered ones too.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Bound.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" The log never holds more than "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"byteBound"},{"type":"text","text":" bytes. When a record wouldn’t fit, the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"oldest segments are deleted until it does, and each one deleted with records not yet"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"delivered yields a "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" on "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/dropReports","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". A record too large for an empty log"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is kept in memory only."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Recovery."}]},{"type":"text","text":" A store opened on a directory recovers the records earlier runs left there"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and a tracker given the store delivers them first. Each segment is cut at its first torn or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"corrupt record, keeping every intact record before it, and the bytes cut off are reported."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"A segment comes back whole, delivered records and all. Each record a delivery had started on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"comes back with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isRedelivered"},{"type":"text","text":" set, as it may have reached a destination already: one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"delivered before the app ended, or one delivered just as it ended, before the store could"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"delete its segment. A record whose delivery mark can’t be written is held back from that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"delivery, so it is never sent twice unannounced, and delivered on a later launch."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Newer versions."}]},{"text":" A segment a newer release of the app wrote, in a later version of the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"format, is left on disk untouched after a rollback, for that release to deliver: this one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"neither reads it nor counts it toward the bound.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Open one store per directory at a time; two would delete each other’s segments. Copies of a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"store share its log.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence"]]},"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/RecordStore","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" that keeps records in a directory of append-only segment files, bounded in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"size, until they are delivered.","type":"text"}],"references":{"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/SegmentStore/directory":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Where the store keeps its segments."}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/directory","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"directory","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"FilePath","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:13SystemPackage8FilePathV"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/segmentstore\/directory","title":"directory"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/SegmentStore/dropReports":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/segmentstore\/dropreports","title":"dropReports","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"dropReports","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AsyncStream","preciseIdentifier":"s:ScS","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"DropReport","preciseIdentifier":"s:11Persistence10DropReportO","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/dropReports","abstract":[{"text":"A report of each drop, in the order they happen, from recovery onwards.","type":"text"}]},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/SegmentStore/synchronize()":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/synchronize()","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"synchronize","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"()","kind":"text"}],"title":"synchronize()","url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/segmentstore\/synchronize()","role":"symbol","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Flushes every segment written since the last flush to storage ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"fsync"},{"type":"text","text":"), so it survives"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"power loss."}]},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/BinaryCodable":{"url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/binarycodable","type":"topic","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","title":"BinaryCodable","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/BinaryCodable","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"BinaryCodable"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A value with a compact binary form, written and read field by field in a fixed order."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"BinaryCodable"}]},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/DropReport":{"url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/dropreport","type":"topic","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport","title":"Dro